  "scenario": "Boot each image with the same DTB. Stop Plasma and alternate two CPU-filled dumb buffers for 2000 nonblocking atomic page flips. Repeat with 2000 explicit GPU submissions. Restore the installed KWin and run the previously measured Qt Quick Vulkan scenes. Measure each scene for 60 seconds after warm-up. Compare the kernel GPU submission worker and its interrupt counters.",
  "expected": "For native KMS, complete 2000 events in about 33 seconds with a median near 16.7 ms and zero DRM and DE errors. With GPU interrupts, observe hardware interrupts, lower submission worker CPU time and no regression in the two Qt interval percentiles.",
  "observed": "Both kernels completed every native flip. The polling and interrupt images took 34.027 and 34.205 seconds. On the same interrupt image a second native run buffered the event log in memory and paused remote SSH polling. All 1999 event sequence increments were one. The event span was 33.305769 s. Each had 1999 fast dumb-buffer updates and one guarded update. Plasma returned on both boots. The Qt Quick clients used Vulkan on PowerVR and reported about 30 swaps per second. KWin composited with OpenGL ES through Zink on the same GPU. In a separate NPU compute check, each image produced 3456 NPU interrupts and the same reference output digest.",
