  "limits": [
    "Both images include the same fast display path. Their difference measures GPU interrupt handling. The previous 118.342 s native result comes from an earlier image and test session.",
    "The native run missed 37 refresh intervals on the polling image and 48 on the interrupt image. Four and five intervals longer than one refresh account for these misses, respectively. The median alone does not establish continuous presentation.",
    "Qt frameSwapped counts describe the application. The separate CRTC observer polls at a lower rate than the HDMI refresh. Neither measurement gives optical display latency.",
    "The GPU CPU counters cover the complete workload window. The Qt window includes the warm-up and observation overhead. An IRQ wait can time out without a DRM or DE fault.",
    "The buffered native run also changed SSH polling. This comparison measures their combined effect. It cannot identify the cause of the periodic pauses.",
    "The NPU workload ran separately from the graphics workload. Its output SHA-256 was e6e8f6d823cc10b77a6db35de3eb587975dbed440648a536f5819ea790216b59."
  ],
